# Test harnesses must not hardcode network ports

We run the workspace with `pnpm -r test` (parallel by default). Two suites that
both spawn `anvil` (or any TCP listener) on the same hardcoded port will
deterministically collide and one will fail with `Connection refused` / `EADDRINUSE`.

## The rule

Any test helper that spawns a process binding a TCP port MUST request a free
port from the OS at startup, not pin a constant. The canonical pattern lives in
`packages/sdk/test/helpers/anvil.ts::pickFreePort`.

## Why ephemeral, not "pick the next one"

- Per-package port offsets (`18545`, `18546`, …) appear safe until a third
  package reuses one or a developer runs the suite alongside an unrelated dev
  server. The failure mode is intermittent and confusing.
- OS-assigned ports (`listen(0)`) are coordination-free. The TOCTOU window
  between closing the probe listener and `anvil` binding is tens of
  milliseconds and the kernel does not aggressively recycle in that window.

## Examples

### BAD

```typescript
const ANVIL_PORT = 18545;
const ANVIL_URL = `http://127.0.0.1:${ANVIL_PORT}`;

const anvil = spawn("anvil", ["--port", String(ANVIL_PORT), ...]);
```

### GOOD

```typescript
import { createServer } from "node:net";

async function pickFreePort(): Promise<number> {
  return new Promise((resolveFn, rejectFn) => {
    const srv = createServer();
    srv.unref();
    srv.on("error", rejectFn);
    srv.listen(0, "127.0.0.1", () => {
      const addr = srv.address();
      if (!addr || typeof addr === "string") {
        srv.close();
        rejectFn(new Error("failed to read ephemeral port"));
        return;
      }
      const port = addr.port;
      srv.close(() => resolveFn(port));
    });
  });
}

const port = await pickFreePort();
const rpcUrl = `http://127.0.0.1:${port}`;
const anvil = spawn("anvil", ["--port", String(port), ...]);
```

## Allowed exception

Tests that need a stable URL across multiple processes (e.g. shelling out to a
CLI that reads a config file written ahead of time) MAY accept an explicit
`port` option, but the DEFAULT must still be ephemeral.
